Date:     Wed, 21 Apr 93 23:37:45 GMT
From: starr@genie.slhs.udel.edu
Subject: Respectability

There are two issues involved with appearing "respectable": the messenger and
the message.  The rule seems to be that people will accept weird messages
from normal messengers, and reject normal messages from strange messengers.
This is what I understand to be the case from the scientific research that's
been done in this area.

So, this means that there is a niche for respectable spokesmen for freedom of
cryptography.  This doesn't mean that there's any need for any compromise in
the pursuit of this liberty, though.

William Lloyd Garrison got it right when he was leading the fight against
slavery: gradualism in theory or rhetoric will mean pepetuity in practice;
radicalism, extremism, or abolitionism in theory or rhetoric will mean
gradualism in practice.  Unless we fight for it all, we won't win anything.

Tim Starr

