Subject: IMMORTALITY: Not

I was thinking about personal immortality, and it's pretty clear that
damn few of us will be around in 1000 years.  Yes, we may come up with
some new form of abundance, but like dropping a bacterium into an
empty ocean, it doesn't take long for exponential growth to fill the
ocean.  Our genes or memes or whatever silicon version thereof we
become in the next centuries will have the nasty tendency to replicate
themselves, and will fill up the living space available sooner or
later.  As somebody mentioned, even the lowest rate of exponential
growth of information will eventually fill a solid ball of organized
matter expanding at the speed of light...

So, what does that imply?  Basically, that a position of complete
egotism is untenable.  I will eventually die, and I'd better give some
thought to what I'd like to leave behind.

